#describe what A Release workflow builds the macOS and Windows packages and attaches them to a tag's GitHub Release.
#describe what It starts on a pushed v* tag or by hand for an existing tag; the steps are documented in the installation guide.
#describe before Packages were built by hand with the package scripts and shared as files.
#describe after Pushing a v* tag, or running the workflow for v0.2.0, yields a release with Lantern-mac.zip and Lantern-win-x64.zip.
#describe verified Typecheck, lint and unit tests pass and the workflow parses as YAML with every action pinned by SHA; the workflow itself has not been run.
+ .github/workflows/release.yml
~ docs/installation.md
#order .github/workflows/release.yml
#order docs/installation.md
#reason .github/workflows/release.yml Releases need packages built on macOS and Windows runners and attached to a tag's GitHub Release without a manual upload.
#reason docs/installation.md Maintainers need the tag-or-manual-run release steps and the ad-hoc signing caveat written down next to the build info.
#story Publishing a release
#step actor A maintainer
#step action pushes a v* tag or runs the Release workflow for an existing tag
